     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384\" data-account-id=\"6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384\" accountid=\"6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Michael Durbin</a>, Could you look at the PR below:<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/pull/693\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/pull/693</a></p>\n\n<p>The fix at the ModeShape level is in. However, I almost like the \"workaround\" logic better than this PR. As you can see, the PR logic creates a version check-point even if the eventual application of the label will fail due to being a duplicate.</p>\n\n<p>What are your thoughts?</p>",
